      "line": 25,
      "message": "`**vault.to_account_info().try_borrow_mut_lamports()? -= a...` in `withdraw` uses `-=` on a value that holds funds. In a release build this wraps silently rather than failing.",
      "references": [
        "https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/overflow-underflow",
        "https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/profiles.html#overflow-checks"
      ],
      "remediation": "Use `checked_add`/`checked_sub`/`checked_mul` and return an error on overflow, or `saturating_*` where clamping is the intended behaviour. Alternatively set `overflow-checks = true` under `[profile.release]`, which turns wrapping into a panic and silences this rule.",
      "rule": "WT003",
      "severity": "high",
      "snippet": "        **vault.to_account_info().try_borrow_mut_lamports()? -= amount;"
